WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.129
A kernel is the smallest part of a computer that everything else has to ask permission from. It is kept small on purpose, because a small thing can be checked.

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:19.538
Until this week, DELPHI was a set of scripts that produced biology. The reasons lived in a document beside the result. Documents rot, and the result stays.

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:30.987
Now there is a kernel, and it knows five moves. Evidence. Fact. Law. Verdict. Build. Nothing else is allowed through.

00:00:31.327 --> 00:00:42.696
Evidence is a quote from a paper, with its page. A fact is one number out of that quote. A law is a theorem, checked by a prover. A verdict is the law applied to the facts.

00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:52.820
The kernel will not hand over a build unless every verdict underneath it holds. When one does not, you get a refusal that names what was missing. The refusing is the feature.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:01:03.229
It can also answer: cannot assess. Two numbers measured in different bacterial strains are not comparable. A tool that compares them quietly is worse than no tool.

00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:14.758
Who needs that. A lab that has to defend a construct it built. A reviewer who wants to see the chain, not the conclusion. A funder asking what a result actually rests on.

00:01:15.098 --> 00:01:29.516
So here is what DELPHI can do now that it could not. Take a logic circuit written in Verilog, the language chip designers use, and compile it into annotated DNA and a protocol a robot can run. Then stop where the published literature runs out.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:40.410
On the numbers one paper printed for its own logic gates, the worst pair has a noise margin of minus two units. That circuit cannot work, and the kernel says so before anyone clones it.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:50.849
The numbers it could not find came out as draft publications, one per missing measurement. That is the shortest list that would unblock the model, so it is the right thing to send an author.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:55.533
All of it reproduces from one command, and the whole chain is on the page.
